// jumpcam — the plate cam from platecam.mech, but now with mass: a 100 g
// follower held on the cam by a spring and gravity, and a contact that can let
// go. This is what a cam does at speed. A kinematic cam assumes the follower
// stays put; a real one only stays on while the spring can accelerate it
// down as fast as the cam surface falls away, and when it cannot, it leaves.
//
//   mech run examples/jumpcam.mech --headless 1
//
// The cam turns 600 rpm. The hard moment is the end of the rise, where the
// surface decelerates hardest (peak 6.28 h / beta^2 x omega^2, about 98 m/s^2)
// and the follower must be pulled down as fast: 9.8 N for 100 g. At the top of
// the lift the spring (200 N/m, stretched 23 mm) plus gravity give only ~5.6 N,
// so the follower leaves the cam near the top of the lift, flies, and lands
// again with an impact. Slow the cam to 300 rpm and the force needed drops 4x
// (2.5 N): the contact never lets go.
//
// Both the cam speed and the spring are parameters, so the threshold can be found by
// asking the tool instead of by hand:
//
//   mech sweep examples/jumpcam.mech --set speed=500:800:25 --time 0.15 --report liftoffs
//   mech sweep examples/jumpcam.mech --set speed=600 --set preload_k=100:400:50 --report liftoffs
//   mech run   examples/jumpcam.mech --headless 1 --set speed=300       (it never lets go)
//
// 'restitution' is Newton's coefficient for the landing: 0 sticks, 1 bounces
// back with the speed it came in at. Every joule is bookkept: the energy
// ledger at the end of the run counts the cam's work, and what each impact
// discarded.
mechanism jumpcam {
  param speed = 600          // cam speed, rpm
  param preload_k = 200      // follower spring stiffness, N/m

  world { gravity: 9.81  step: 0.0005 }

  ground frame {
    anchor axle at (0, 0)
    anchor rail at (0, 0.031) dir (0, 1)     // starts on the cam: base 25 + roller 6 mm
  }

  shaft cam at frame.axle
  cam lobe on cam.A {
    base   0.025
    roller 0.006
    rise 0.012 over 100 deg cycloidal
    dwell 60 deg
    return over 140 deg modtrap
    dwell
  }

  body follower {
    anchor tip at (0, 0) dir (1, 0)
    mass: 0.1
  }
  slide follower.tip -> frame.rail
  spring preload follower.tip -> frame.axle { k: preload_k  rest: 0.020 }
  touch follower.tip on lobe restitution 0.3

  drive cam at speed rpm
}
